conftypes.h knows arm64 (aarch64 port, task A16)

The MACOSX branch defines HOSTTYPE per __ARCH__ macro and falls back to CONF_HOSTTYPE for
anything it does not recognise. It has no arm64 case, and cider's generated bash flags set
CONF_MACHTYPE/OSTYPE/VENDOR but not CONF_HOSTTYPE (unused on x86_64, where the __x86_64__
case wins), so an arm64 guest build hits "use of undeclared identifier 'CONF_HOSTTYPE'" in
variables.c. Add the case the way the others read; __arm64__ is the guest compiler's spelling.

--- a/bash-3.2/conftypes.h
+++ b/bash-3.2/conftypes.h
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@
 #    define HOSTTYPE "i386"
 #  elif defined(__arm__)
 #    define HOSTTYPE "arm"
+#  elif defined(__arm64__) || defined(__aarch64__)
+#    define HOSTTYPE "arm64"
 #  else
 #    define HOSTTYPE CONF_HOSTTYPE
 #  endif
